.TH SYS_VM_BUFFERS 2 "2026-05-09" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_vm_buffers \- query buffer cache statistics
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_vm_buffers(sys_bufinfo_t *" buf ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_vm_buffers ()
fills
.I *buf
with bio cache buffer statistics:
.PP
.RS
.nf
typedef struct sys_bufinfo {
    uint64_t nr_buffers;
    uint64_t buffer_size;   /* bytes per buffer */
    uint64_t dirty;
    uint64_t writeback;
} sys_bufinfo_t;
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B buffer_size
is reported as
.B PAGE_SIZE
(4096).  The other fields are zero today; they begin populating
once the bio subsystem grows a public stats accessor.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success; on failure -1 and
.I errno
is set per the error contract.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I buf
is NULL.
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I buf
points outside the caller's address space.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_vm_stats (2),
.BR sys_vm_info (2),
.BR sys_vm_slabs (2)
